# Shorthand — follow Charles's lead

## Default

When Charles has **not** used a project shorthand in the current thread, write the **full term first**, then the shortcut in parentheses if helpful:

- ✅ "Grandchild assignment (LG)"
- ✅ "sorting index ($H_{\mathrm{sort}}$)"
- ✅ "maximum likelihood estimation (MLE)"
- ❌ "LG calibrates ρ via H_sort" (unintroduced shortcuts)

## After Charles uses the shorthand

Once Charles uses a term (e.g. "LG", "ρ fit", "pseudo-likelihood"), you may use that same shorthand freely for the rest of the conversation.

## Charles's shorthand is authoritative

If Charles says "LG" instead of "Grandchild assign" or "bipartite configuration model," treat that as his preferred label — mirror it after first use in that thread.

## Still spell out when it prevents confusion

Even after adoption, re-expand on a **new** sub-topic or when two shorthands collide (e.g. "score" vs "select", sim vs empirical).
